  <subsection>
    <title>Wednesday 8/24</title>

<ol>
  <li>
    <p>
      The region bounded by <m>y = \sqrt{x}</m> and the <m>x</m>-axis between <m>x = 0</m> and <m>x = 4</m>.
      Rotate around the <m>x</m>-axis.
    </p>
  </li>

  <li>
    <p>
      The region bounded by <m>y = \sqrt{x}</m>, the <m>y</m>-axis, and <m>y = 4</m>.
      Rotate around the <m>y</m>-axis.
    </p>
  </li>

  <li>
    <p>
      The region bounded by <m>y = \sqrt{x}</m> and the <m>x</m>-axis between <m>x = 0</m> and <m>x = 4</m>.
      Rotate around the <m>y</m>-axis.
    </p>
  </li>

  <li>
    <p>
      The region enclosed by <m>y = \sqrt{x}</m> and <m>y = x^{4}</m>.
      Rotate around the line <m>y = 5</m>.
    </p>
  </li>

  <li>
    <p>
      Challenge 1: Repeat #4, but rotate around the line <m>y = -5</m>.
    </p>
  </li>

  <li>
    <p>
      Challenge 2: The 3D shape whose cross sections perpendicular to the <m>x</m>-axis are squares with side length <m>\sqrt{x}</m>, from <m>x = 1</m> to <m>x = 4</m>.
    </p>
  </li>
</ol>

    <p>
